From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] riscv64: recognize the platform and give OpenBLAS a TARGET

v0.3.27.44.x predates upstream's own riscv64 support by about two years:
get_plat_tag() doesn't know the plat name, and do_build_lib()'s TARGET
case statement has no Linux-riscv64 entry, so OpenBLAS's getarch.c
("This arch/CPU is not supported by OpenBLAS") is never even reached -
the build fails earlier, in this wrapper script.

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://github.com/MacPython/openblas-libs/commit/6d72d214d479976e382a83e7100e88ee7df964c6]

Upstream's own "Build riscv64+glibc wheel" backports as TARGET=GENERIC,
which this patch tried first - it compiles, but fails on real riscv64
hardware here with "'sgemm_p' undeclared" from param.h's SGEMM_DEFAULT_P
macro: OpenBLAS's plain GENERIC target has no riscv64 kernel-parameter
block in this release's param.h at all. TARGET=RISCV64_GENERIC (the
rv64gc baseline OpenBLAS has shipped since well before 0.3.27, confirmed
in OpenMathLib/OpenBLAS's own v0.3.27 tag: getarch.c's
FORCE_RISCV64_GENERIC and a real param.h RISCV64_GENERIC block defining
SGEMM_DEFAULT_P etc.) is what upstream's own newer releases use for this
case once they special-case riscv64 away from the x86/power/arm generic
fallback - confirmed working here from a real riscv64 build.
---
 tools/build_steps.sh | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tools/build_steps.sh b/tools/build_steps.sh
index baaa182..316f351 100644
--- a/tools/build_steps.sh
+++ b/tools/build_steps.sh
@@ -33,7 +33,7 @@ function get_plat_tag {
     local mb_ml_ver=${MB_ML_VER:-1}
     local mb_ml_libc=${MB_ML_LIBC:-manylinux}
     case $plat in
-        i686|x86_64|arm64|universal2|intel|aarch64|s390x|ppc64le) ;;
+        i686|x86_64|arm64|universal2|intel|aarch64|s390x|ppc64le|riscv64) ;;
         *) echo Did not recognize plat $plat; return 1 ;;
     esac
     local uname=${2:-$(uname)}
@@ -148,6 +148,10 @@ function do_build_lib {
             local bitness=64
             local target="POWER8"
             ;;
+        Linux-riscv64)
+            local bitness=64
+            local target="RISCV64_GENERIC"
+            ;;
         *) echo "Strange plat value $plat"; exit 1 ;;
     esac
     case $interface64 in
